1. INTRODUCTION

This report documents the activities carried out during the Practicum period of the Professional Certificate SEAG0211 – Environmental Management, developed in the Quality and Environment Department of Maetel, a company specialized in engineering, construction and operation of energy facilities.

The objective of this Practicum was to apply knowledge acquired in environmental management within real processes of a company certified in international environmental standards.

---

2. PRACTICUM OBJECTIVES

2.1 General Objectives

- Integrate theoretical knowledge of environmental management in a professional environment
- Participate in environmental control, monitoring and documentation processes
- Understand the operation of management systems based on ISO standards
- Develop technical competencies in document analysis, environmental matrices and internal procedures

2.2 Specific Objectives

- Review environmental indicators and detect discrepancies
- Update internal and external documentation related to environmental management
- Collaborate in preparation of future ISO 14001 audits, developing points included in the most recent report and participate in documentation preparation for the environmental department during ISO 37001, 37002 and 37301 audits
- Draft regulatory amendments for conditioned Environmental Impact Assessments (EIA) and environmental technical notes
- Participate in department working groups and meetings

---

3. DESCRIPTION OF ORGANIZATION AND DEPARTMENT

Maetel, belonging to the VINCI/Cobra IS Group, develops energy, infrastructure and industrial services projects. The Quality and Environment Department manages regulatory compliance, corresponding ISO certifications, waste management, environmental aspect analysis and any other environmental documentation for renewable energy projects nationwide and internationally, as well as other facilities.

---

4. ACTIVITIES PERFORMED

4.1 Quantitative Environmental Report – Semester 1

- Review of environmental indicators registered in internal system for Carbon Footprint calculation
- Identification and correction of discrepancies in data from Spain, United Arab Emirates and Saudi Arabia facilities
- Verification of consistency between records, evidence and documentation

4.2 ISO 14001 Audit

- Analysis of certification renewal audit report
- Review of non-conformities and improvement recommendations
- Update of requirement control and applicable compliance obligation procedures
- Drafting of instructions for completion of requirements matrix
- Creation of new format specific to projects
- Update of applicable environmental legislation list
- Improvement of context analysis (SWOT) incorporating:
  • Documented evidence
  • PESTEL analysis
  • Terminology compliant with ISO 14001:2026

4.3 ISO 37001, 37002 and 37301 Audits

- Collection of Environmental area documentation: contracts, invoices, AAIs (Aspect and Impact Analysis), waste management and transport authorizations
- Creation of waste management and transport provider control document
- Design of matrix with fields: Area · Provider · Regional Community · Tax ID · Required Documentation
- Automation of authorization search using formula linked to regional government portals
- Attendance at audit as observer

4.4 External Documentation

- Drafting of environmental technical note on compensatory measures for ENEL Green Power photovoltaic cluster
- Drafting and review of amendment requesting modification of vegetation fence plan, with technical and environmental justification
- Drafting and review of second amendment for another cluster project
- Active participation in associated working group

4.5 Internal Documentation

- Review of procedure for significant environmental aspects analysis and its matrix
- Update of waste management procedure (regulatory updates and editing)
- Update of applicable legislation list and other stakeholder obligations, as well as its procedure and compliance control matrix
- Review and editing of department welcome email for new employees
- Redesign of Environmental Best Practices in Office document and signage

