5. COMPETENCIES ACQUIRED

5.1 Technical Competencies

- Interpretation and application of environmental regulation
- Management of environmental and legal compliance matrices
- Drafting of technical documentation (notes, amendments, procedures and other formats)
- Document preparation and format design for ISO audits
- Analysis of environmental indicators and detection of inconsistencies
- Use of internal document management tools

5.2 Transversal Competencies

- Organization and time management
- Teamwork in multidisciplinary environments
- Technical written communication
- Analytical capacity and problem-solving ability
- Adaptation to corporate procedures and ISO methodologies

---

6. PERSONAL ASSESSMENT OF PRACTICUM

The Practicum proved to be a highly enriching experience, allowing me to apply certificate knowledge in a real and demanding environment. I was able to participate in key processes of the environmental management system, understand the importance of document traceability and acquire direct experience in audits and ISO procedures.

I particularly highlight the opportunity to draft environmental technical documentation and collaborate in updating internal procedures, tasks that reinforced my analytical capacity and precision in writing with technical language.

---

7. CONCLUSIONS

The Practicum period fully met the formative objectives of the SEAG0211 certificate. The experience at Maetel allowed me to develop essential technical and professional competencies for the environmental management field, as well as understand the real functioning of management systems and auditing procedures in an energy sector company.
